{"key":"CollabTestWindow","text":"## CollabTestWindow\n\nThe **Collab Video Test** is an engineering bench for the shared-screen\nexperiment: it measures how much frame rate the browser loses while streaming\nthe desktop, and lets two tabs on the same account join a test session.\nExpect numbers, not polish.\n\n---\n\n@layout\nCapture Status | 0.50, 0.08 | Whether the browser can capture the canvas. In the Unity Editor this always reads NOT supported; run a WebGL build.\nBenchmark | 0.50, 0.30 | Run Benchmark measures Unity fps with capture off, at full resolution, and at half resolution, then prints the three results.\nManual Controls | 0.50, 0.50 | Start and Stop the capture by hand, and Scale x1, x2, x4 to change the encoder downscale.\nSession | 0.50, 0.80 | Connect joins a Phase 0 session under your account and lists the participants seen.\n\n---\n\n### Shortcuts\n\n- None.\n\n### Status: Planned\n### Purpose: OS","screenshot":""}